YANI: We could just put the death threat back into
pudding farming, as a "fix".

Something in one of the overlong drifted thread
discussions ongoing about "game balance" brought
this to mind:

Some fraction of the time when puddings split, they
should split to something entirely other than
puddings, and fail to respect past possible
genocides when doing so. Splitting a pudding with a
-3 dented pot as ones weilded weapon would be a
whole lot more "interesting" if the children were a
master mind flayer and an arch lich, for example.

A 0.5% chance of getting some selection of two of
the most difficult monsters which can currently be
generated, instead of child puddings with nearly no
HPs, would make pudding farming a thing one did for
limited periods and at substantial risk, to balance
the potential death drop and sacrifice fodder
rewards of pudding farming.

Conceptualize puddings as big wobbly chaos-inside
eggs from which bad news sometimes hatches, if it
helps you swallow this idea.

This would leave the _fun_ of pudding farming
intact, while taking away the "makes a gift of the
game" aspects.

xanthian.

